@AP I’d say the biggest advantage of our Marianas LightSheet is that it’s mounted on a standard inverted microscope. This allows you to image from below, in addition to the lightsheet, for example using a spinning disk, or TIRF, including photomanipulation options or other imaging modalities. It also features a regular XY stage with plenty of space for petridishes. Here is a link to our current brochure <https://www.intelligent-imaging.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/MLS-Brochure.pdf>

For cleared specimen, you can use the multi-immersion dipping objectives from ASI, <https://asiimaging.com/docs/multi-immersion_objectives>. Not for a whole mouse, as it is limited in depth (working distance), but for example, you could easily image a massively expanded brain slice

